			"faq_usdt_title": "What is USDT and how do I use it?",
			"faq_usdt_body": "<strong>USDT (Tether)</strong> is a stablecoin — a digital dollar. Each USDT is worth exactly $1. It runs on the <strong>Binance Smart Chain (BSC)</strong> network, which means transactions are fast and cheap (often under $0.10).",
			"faq_usdt_bullet_1": "<strong>Send USDT</strong> — Enter a BSC address and the amount in dollars. The app routes it on-chain.",
			"faq_usdt_bullet_2": "<strong>Receive USDT</strong> — Select the USDT tab, share your BSC address or generate an invoice. The payer sends USDT from any supported chain.",
			"faq_usdt_bullet_3": "<strong>Swap with rBTC</strong> — You can convert between rBTC (Rootstock Bitcoin) and USDT using built-in swap routes (LI.FI or Symbiosis). This lets you pay for services in whichever currency the other person prefers.",
			"faq_ownwallet_title": "Can I use my own wallet (MetaMask, Ledger)?",
			"faq_ownwallet_body": "Yes. You can <strong>connect your own wallet</strong> — MetaMask, WalletConnect, Trezor, or Ledger — from the Connected tab. This lets you:",
